35,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,- **Benjamin**: The basin survived; the apron didn’t. And half the avenue trees died from neglect. Drawings are cheap; maintenance is expensive.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Misaki,,"The clay is a problem, but shallow work is fine. The real issue is the centre and gate can’t be hoarded.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Mio,,"Oh no, the ledger says planted ground costs triple! And the fund won’t pay for paving. This is a financial trap!","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"Seven staff, not eighteen. But two volunteer groups are already active. One handles habitat, the other sports. That’s a real, existing workforce.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Minako,,"The data is clear. People need firm ground to cross, and the heat and drainage are already failing. We must design for that reality.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Mio, triple the cost is a disaster. @Minako, if the ground is failing, we can’t just plant more. We need durable infrastructure.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Mio"",""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Misaki,,"@Benjamin, durable infrastructure is good, but the clay makes deep work risky. @Minako, the centre can’t be hoarded, so we must plan for continuous access.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Benjamin"",""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Mio,,"@Benjamin, wait! The fund pays for planting, not paving! If we build hard surfaces, we lose two-thirds of the money. That’s the real trap!","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Mio, the fund terms are critical. @Minako, the volunteer groups already cover sports and habitat. We need a plan that fits their existing capacity, not just the budget.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Mio"",""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Minako,,"@Mio, the fund terms are a hard constraint. @Asuka, the volunteer groups are vital, but the drainage failure is immediate. We need a plan that respects both the budget and the ground.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Mio"",""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Misaki, the apron failed because it was hard. The basin survived because it was water. I’m leaning toward the wetland, not the plaza.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Misaki,,"@Benjamin, water is risky with this clay. @Mio, if the fund only pays for planting, we must avoid heavy surfacing.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Benjamin"",""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Mio,,"@Benjamin, I agree! The wetland fits the fund perfectly. Plus, the ledger shows hard surfaces are cheaper to keep. We must avoid the plaza!","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"@Benjamin, the basin surviving proves water works. @Mio, the fund constraint is absolute. We need a plan that uses the existing volunteer habitat group, not just cheap paving.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Benjamin"",""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Minako,,"@Benjamin, the basin surviving is key. @Mio, the fund constraint is absolute. We need a plan that respects the ground and the budget.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Benjamin"",""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,"@Misaki, the clay risk is real, but the basin proved water management works. I’m leaning toward the wetland, provided we can phase it without hoarding the centre.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Misaki,,"@Benjamin, the clay makes deep excavation risky, but shallow work is quoted at ordinary rates. If we keep the wetland shallow, the ground should hold.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Mio,,"@Benjamin, exactly! The wetland uses the fund money properly. Plus, the ledger says hard surfaces are cheaper to keep, so we avoid the plaza trap!","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Asuka,,"@Benjamin, the habitat volunteer group is already active. A wetland plan fits their existing capacity perfectly. We have the workforce ready.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Minako,,"@Benjamin, the drainage data confirms the wetland is the only logical fix. It addresses the immediate failure and respects the fund. I support it.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
